<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/pipeline-coding-autonomy.css">
<section class="pipeline-panel" id="pipelineCodingAutonomy" aria-labelledby="codingAutonomyTitle">
  <div class="pipeline-panel-header"><div><span class="pipeline-run-label">Automatic corrections · live tracking</span><h3 id="codingAutonomyTitle">Coding Team autonomy</h3><p>Approved tasks only. The team updates draft PRs, watches CI and corrects within your budgets.</p></div><button type="button" class="pipeline-btn compact" id="codingAutonomyRefresh">Refresh</button></div>
  <div class="pipeline-autonomy-body">
  <p id="codingAutonomyStatus" role="status" aria-live="polite">Reading Core's autonomy state…</p>
  <label class="pipeline-autonomy-confirm"><input type="checkbox" id="codingAutonomyConfirm"> I approve this bounded task scope and the selected campaign</label>
  <div class="pipeline-autonomy-actions">
    <button type="button" class="pipeline-btn compact" data-autonomy-switch="true">Enable authorized scope</button>
    <button type="button" class="pipeline-btn compact" data-autonomy-switch="false">Pause new work and corrections</button>
  </div>
  <p class="pipeline-subtle">Pausing prevents new workers and corrections. Stop a running worker from its task card. Human review, merge, installation and product acceptance are separate decisions.</p>
  <section class="pipeline-report-continuation" id="reportContinuation" aria-labelledby="reportContinuationTitle">
    <h4 id="reportContinuationTitle">Private reports continue automatically</h4>
    <p class="pipeline-subtle">When a report execution runs out of calls or time with its work saved, Core starts the next execution from that exact report, inside the grant and campaign window you already approved. It never extends a grant, never retries another kind of stop, and alerts you when a report is blocked, makes no progress or needs a new grant or window.</p>
    <p id="reportContinuationStatus" role="status" aria-live="polite">Reading the continuation switch…</p>
    <label class="pipeline-autonomy-confirm"><input type="checkbox" id="reportContinuationConfirm"> I approve continuing saved reports within their existing grants</label>
    <div class="pipeline-autonomy-actions">
      <button type="button" class="pipeline-btn compact" data-report-continuation="true">Continue reports automatically</button>
      <button type="button" class="pipeline-btn compact" data-report-continuation="false">Pause automatic continuation</button>
    </div>
    <form id="reportEscalationForm" class="pipeline-report-escalation">
      <h4>Cloud escalation of failed report steps</h4>
      <p class="pipeline-subtle">After a step group fails once on the local model, the runner sends that group's documents and the source files they cite to a cloud model in one request, then verifies every cited line as for any step. Only tasks whose report grant allows it are affected. Models are tried in order; one OpenClaw cannot call directly is skipped.</p>
      <p id="reportEscalationStatus" role="status" aria-live="polite">Reading the escalation policy…</p>
      <label>Models in order, one per line <textarea name="models" rows="2" id="reportEscalationModels"></textarea></label>
      <label>Cost cap per task (USD) <input name="maxCostUsdPerTask" id="reportEscalationCap" type="number" min="0" max="1000" step="0.5"></label>
      <label class="pipeline-autonomy-confirm"><input type="checkbox" id="reportEscalationConfirm"> I approve sending failed step context to these cloud models for tasks that allow it</label>
      <div class="pipeline-autonomy-actions">
        <button type="submit" class="pipeline-btn compact" data-report-escalation="true">Turn escalation on with these settings</button>
        <button type="button" class="pipeline-btn compact" data-report-escalation="false">Turn escalation off</button>
      </div>
    </form>
  </section>
  <details id="codingAutonomySetup">
    <summary>Set up a campaign and authorize a task</summary>
    <p>Only low-risk public engineering work routed to agentx-coding is eligible. Review the files and budgets before approving. Ideas and private/family tasks stay outside this control.</p>
    <form id="codingAutonomyCampaign">
      <fieldset><legend>1. Open the reserved campaign window</legend>
      <p class="pipeline-subtle">Reserve and review a coding campaign in <a href="/cluster-schedule">Cluster Schedule</a>, then enter its ID here. Work requires an active permitted window.</p>
      <p><label>Reserved coding campaign ID <input name="queueRequestId" required></label>
        <button type="submit" class="pipeline-btn compact">Begin the approved campaign window</button></p></fieldset>
    </form>
    <form id="codingAutonomyAuthorize">
      <fieldset><legend>2. Review the exact task and files</legend>
      <p><label>Task ID <input name="pipelineId" pattern="[0-9]{4}" maxlength="4" placeholder="Four-digit task ID" required></label></p>
      <p><label>Approved heavy-work campaign ID <input name="queueRequestId" required></label></p>
      <p><label>Exact permitted files, one per line <textarea name="scope" rows="4" required></textarea></label></p>
      <p><label>Independent verification <select name="verificationProfile">
        <option value="agentx-dispatcher-tests/v1">Coding integration tests</option>
        <option value="agentx-core-runner-tests/v1">Bounded Core coding tests</option>
        <option value="agentx-benchmark-artifact-tests/v1">Benchmark artifact comparison tests</option>
      </select></label></p></fieldset>
      <fieldset><legend>3. Set cumulative work limits</legend>
      <p class="pipeline-subtle">These are total budgets for this authorization, including corrections.</p>
      <p><label>Maximum corrections <input name="maxResumes" type="number" min="0" max="2" value="2" required></label>
        <label>Total work minutes <input name="workMinutes" type="number" min="1" max="240" value="240" required></label>
        <label>Total test minutes <input name="testMinutes" type="number" min="1" max="80" value="80" required></label>
        <label>Total model minutes <input name="modelMinutes" type="number" min="1" max="90" value="90" required></label>
        <label>Total model calls <input name="modelCalls" type="number" min="1" max="128" value="128" required></label>
        <label>Total CI waiting minutes <input name="ciMinutes" type="number" min="1" max="60" value="60" required></label>
        <label>Minutes without useful progress <input name="noProgressMinutes" type="number" min="1" max="45" value="45" required></label></p></fieldset>
      <button type="submit" class="pipeline-btn compact">Authorize this task and file scope</button>
    </form>
  </details>
  <h4 class="pipeline-autonomy-tasks-title">Current Coding Team tasks</h4>
  <div id="codingAutonomyTasks"></div>
  <a class="pipeline-autonomy-history-link" href="#pipelineHistory">Archived tasks and qualifications <i class="fas fa-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
  </div>
</section>
<script src="/js/pipeline-coding-autonomy.js" defer></script>
<script src="/js/pipeline-report-continuation.js" defer></script>
